WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.149
This closing module brings the OWASP Top 10 back to the HIPAA Security Rule.

2
00:00:05.149 --> 00:00:21.071
In a healthcare application, security defects are not just technical issues; they can affect electronic protected health information, patient trust, clinical workflows, and the evidence an organization relies on during risk management.

3
00:00:21.071 --> 00:00:26.898
Use the OWASP categories as a practical way to discuss where application risk appears.

4
00:00:26.898 --> 00:00:44.243
Broken access control, weak authentication, cryptographic failures, injection, insecure design, vulnerable components, logging gaps, and server-side request forgery can all create paths to unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or disruption of ePHI.

5
00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:50.950
The HIPAA connection is strongest when engineering work is tied to concrete safeguards and records.

6
00:00:50.950 --> 00:01:09.582
Access reviews, server-side authorization checks, encryption decisions, secure configuration, dependency management, audit logging, monitoring, incident response, and risk analysis should produce evidence that security, privacy, compliance, and legal stakeholders can review.

7
00:01:09.582 --> 00:01:15.273
This course is an awareness and planning aid, not a formal compliance determination.

8
00:01:15.273 --> 00:01:28.756
Validate specific safeguard mappings with qualified HIPAA stakeholders, document the decisions, and keep improving the application security program as systems, threats, and business processes change.

